# Line endings — pin correct EOL on checkout regardless of the platform the
# repo is cloned on. Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which CRLF's
# shell scripts and breaks them (#!/usr/bin/env bash → /bin/bash\r not found);
# PowerShell wants the opposite.
#
# Order matters: for a given file the LAST matching pattern wins, so the
# specific patterns below must come after the `*` default.

# Default: treat everything else as text, normalized to LF in the repo and
# converted per-platform on checkout (keeps markdown/json/docs stable).
* text=auto

# Shell scripts and plain-text files must always be LF so they run correctly
# on Linux/WSL no matter where the checkout happens.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts must always be CRLF to run from a Windows host.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
